you mean different ways/frameworks to integrate Kafka with Spring, such as Raw Kafka API, Spring Kafka Starter, and Spring Cloud Stream.

1. Raw Kafka — kafka-clients

You directly use Apache Kafka's Java client.

Dependency:

<dependency>
    <groupId>org.apache.kafka</groupId>
    <artifactId>kafka-clients</artifactId>
</dependency>

You manually create:

KafkaProducer
KafkaConsumer
ProducerRecord
ConsumerRecord

Example:

KafkaProducer<String, String> producer = ...
producer.send(new ProducerRecord<>("orders", "Hello"));

➡️ Most control, but more boilerplate.

2. Spring Kafka — spring-kafka

Dependency:

<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.kafka</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-kafka</artifactId>
</dependency>

You get:

KafkaTemplate
@KafkaListener
ConsumerFactory
ProducerFactory

Example:

kafkaTemplate.send("orders", "Hello");
@KafkaListener(topics = "orders")
public void consume(String message) {
    System.out.println(message);
}

➡️ Most common choice for Spring Boot applications.

3. Spring Cloud Stream Kafka

Dependencies:

<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-cloud-stream</artifactId>
</dependency>

<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-cloud-stream-binder-kafka</artifactId>
</dependency>

Instead of directly working with Kafka APIs, you work with messages/bindings.

For example:

@Bean
public Consumer<String> orderConsumer() {
    return message -> {
        System.out.println(message);
    };
}

Configuration connects that consumer to Kafka.

➡️ Higher abstraction; useful when you want to make your application less tightly coupled to Kafka.

4. Spring Cloud Stream + Kafka Streams

If you need stream processing, you can use Kafka Streams through Spring Cloud Stream.

Typical use cases:

Kafka Topic A
     ↓
Filter / Transform
     ↓
Join / Aggregate
     ↓
Kafka Topic B

Good for:

Filtering
Transformation
Aggregation
Joins
Stateful stream processing


Easy interview comparison
| Approach                | Dependency                           | Abstraction       | Control |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ----------------- | ------- |
| **Raw Kafka**           | `kafka-clients`                      | Low               | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐   |
| **Spring Kafka**        | `spring-kafka`                       | Medium            | ⭐⭐⭐⭐    |
| **Spring Cloud Stream** | `spring-cloud-stream` + Kafka binder | High              | ⭐⭐⭐     |
| **Kafka Streams**       | Kafka Streams / Cloud Stream binder  | Stream processing | ⭐⭐⭐⭐    |


Interview answer:

"We can integrate Kafka with Spring Boot in different ways. We can use the raw Kafka client for low-level control,
Spring Kafka for native Spring integration using KafkaTemplate and @KafkaListener,
or Spring Cloud Stream with the Kafka binder for a higher-level messaging abstraction. For stream processing, we can use Kafka Streams."